This directory is intended for project header files.

A header file is a file containing C declarations and macro definitions
to be shared between several project source files. You request the use of a
header file in your project source file by including it, with the C
preprocessing directive #include.

For example, if you put a header file "myheader.h" in this directory, you can
then have source files inside your local "src" directory that #include it:

    #include "myheader.h"

Headers that are private to the firmware belong here. Anything that is a
reusable, self-contained library belongs in lib/ instead.

Note: stm32_assert.h lives here because the STM32Cube HAL/LL drivers include it
unconditionally when USE_FULL_ASSERT is defined.